# PROF-CTL: the op-level device profile of the PRODUCTION profile (no W1 or production profile has ever been profiled). Eight seats: eight real-text coding users at 4,096 tokens each (ops_profile_plan fixes the shape and
# takes eight users on an eight-seat profile), user 0 asked for 256 tokens and the rest for 128, an unprofiled twin first (ops-twin: the texts and the unperturbed round times) and then the tracy arm (ops-trace) at
# op-support 20000: ops_profile_plan REFUSES any larger count (200000 segfaulted the dispatch thread on three runs). Both verify audits are off on the production profile, as the plan requires. READ: the twin and the trace arm PASS,
# ops/tp4-profile-report.json and cpp_device_perf_report.csv.gz in the artifact, the trace texts equal the twin's (a difference is a FAIL to look at, never to blame on the profiler first). Attribution only: not a timing result.
# THIS IS A PROFILE OF THE UNSALTED PATH: the job sets no C2_GATE_SALT, so fail-closed tenancy leaves prefix reuse off in the profiled arm and production's salted capture and publish work is NOT in the profile. It is also the first profiler attach at eight seats with full 262k reservations; its 130 min is the four-seat figure.
# THE 32K SHAPE IS NOT IN THIS JOB: the plan has no 32k shape (docs/tp4-profile.md: 4k, not 32k, the exactness divergence at 32k and above is unresolved) and op-support 20000 loses the packed rounds at 32k (v133).
# NEVER CANCEL A RUNNING PROFILE JOB: a cancel skips the hand-back step and leaves root-owned logs (the next checkout dies with EACCES); the docker timeout ends it. If it was cancelled anyway, run the driver's cleanup first.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production ENGINE: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's; production's thin layer on top of it is NOT exercised) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
